<title>UK: Regan's Galileo placed in solvent liquidation.</title>
<headline>Regan's Galileo placed in solvent liquidation.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Galileo Group, the special vehicle set up by entrepreneur Andrew Regan and his backers to bid abortively for Britain's Co-operative Wholesale Society was placed in solvent liquidation on Wednesday, accountancy firm Ernst &amp; Young said.</p>
<p>&quot;There are sufficient assets to repay the creditors in full and enable a return to be made to shareholders,&quot; Jason Elles, the Ernst &amp; Young partner appointed as liquidator, said in a statement. This followed a Galileo board meeting to wind up the business with shareholder agreement.</p>
</text>
